module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.remediator_read_as_admission_order

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data remediator_read_as_admission_order: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "remediator_read_as_admission_order" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a remediator on a mutable subject is read as establishing admission ORDER.** THE INVALID STATE: a serialized generated projection is derived somewhere other than inside the transaction that advances main, so main can hold AUTHORITY AND PROJECTION FROM DIFFERENT STATES. THE HARM, measured rather than predicted (2026-09-03): projection-touching pull requests merge one at a time BY HAND, because each merge invalidates every other lane's regeneration, and the cost is paid in re-run floors and operator attention rather than in a wrong answer. DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the reason this is its own class rather than an instance of the merge-staleness class gunbc.merge_lifecycle already owns: a projection is not an independent authority that could carry a receipt of its own -- it is a FUNCTION of the composed authority -- so the well-formed subject is a candidate holding both, and a mechanism whose subject is a MUTABLE BRANCH cannot be that candidate no matter how correct its bytes are. RECOGNITION RULE: for a mechanism proposed as the place a generated projection is derived, ask (1) is its subject the exact tree that could advance main, and (2) can another principal advance main between its derivation and that advance. Two noes are required; the heal-generated-artifacts job answers no to both, which is why its own authority classifies it as a remediator, excludes it from the required aggregate, and records that its pushed head needs revalidation. A human announce, a dashboard-derived freeze roster and an advisory lease all fail (2) and are therefore not terminal repairs either. A SECOND FORM OF THE SAME MISREAD, and the one that costs the most: a shard or freeze rule written over an OBSERVED FILE LIST rather than over the derived resource. A four-path freeze declared on 2026-09-03 blocked a lane whose authority closure did not intersect at all, and the inverse admits two ledgers with disjoint filenames that share one generator. Path-disjointness is not a closure proof in either direction. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- stale projections are writable and cycles are wasted, but the generated-artifact merge driver refuses a diverged projection and the read-only `generated-artifact` required phase refuses drift, so the harm is contained rather than silent. CEILING: mechanically preventable, with the reason -- an admission slot is a fact about a coordinator's behaviour over time, which no constructor here can make unwritable. THE DRIVER AND THE READ-ONLY GATE ARE RETAINED ON THE CLIMB rather than dissolved by it: moving generation inside admission changes what they are evidence about, from a late detector of predictable invalidation into the VERIFIER of admission-produced bytes. NEXT TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: an enforced admission slot that excludes another main advance for the transaction's critical window (an enforced merge queue or an admission coordinator), together with a production producer that composes the candidate, derives the projection inside it, and advances the trunk atomically. The transaction, its refusal arms including the non-total authority composition, and the slot-exclusion partition are modeled and executed in gunbc.projection_admission_transaction with test.claim.projection_admission_transaction_witness, where eligibility is an exhaustive match over gunbc.generated_artifact so a new artifact refuses to compile until it is classified. THE SHARD RULE IS DELIBERATELY NOT MODELED THERE: a closure supplied by hand is a presumption wearing a parameter, so the rule above is a recognition rule only until it can be keyed on v2.lens.module_graph, and the starting policy is global serialization, which needs no classifier. The model is not the enforcement, and the hand queue remains the honest interim mitigation until the trigger lands.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
